Why?

263
00:14:37,793 --> 00:14:40,346
What in this world could
inspire such cruelty?

264
00:14:45,920 --> 00:14:47,980
Not one damn thing.

265
00:14:50,500 --> 00:14:51,330
That...

266
00:14:51,413 --> 00:14:52,680
that's your answer?

267
00:14:57,420 --> 00:14:59,060
The simple truth.

268
00:14:59,320 --> 00:15:02,026
We were chosen by heaven
to punish the humans.

269
00:15:02,780 --> 00:15:04,220
That's our purpose.

270
00:15:07,860 --> 00:15:10,520
And we have the power to do so.

271
00:15:13,580 --> 00:15:18,580
I understand now this
sick and pathetic truth.

272
00:15:25,240 --> 00:15:32,120
All of their fury, their hatred, it doesn't
come from experience or logic or fact.

273
00:15:34,800 --> 00:15:36,920
They have no substance.

274
00:15:40,680 --> 00:15:42,680
Just empty cruelty.

275
00:15:49,920 --> 00:15:54,240
Their hatred, it doesn't come
from experience or logic or fact.

276
00:15:54,540 --> 00:15:58,860
They have no substance, just
empty cruelty. So now what?

277
00:15:59,120 --> 00:16:02,097
I get what he's saying, but how
are they going to stop them?

278
00:16:02,180 --> 00:16:03,797
Hey, what are you standing around for?

279
00:16:03,880 --> 00:16:05,777
We've got to get off the island right now!

280
00:16:05,860 --> 00:16:07,997
I can see the shadow of the Nua already!

281
00:16:08,080 --> 00:16:09,609
It's right over our heads!

282
00:16:15,760 --> 00:16:17,040
Hurry, Whip Hachi!

283
00:16:20,440 --> 00:16:21,717
What's happening?

284
00:16:21,800 --> 00:16:24,329
It looks even more
frightening than before.

285
00:16:29,760 --> 00:16:31,880
Humans are worthless.

286
00:16:32,300 --> 00:16:33,677
Evil creatures.

287
00:16:33,760 --> 00:16:35,517
Never forget that, Heart.

288
00:16:35,600 --> 00:16:36,760
They're scum.

289
00:16:37,200 --> 00:16:40,020
Barely fit to serve us.

290
00:16:44,780 --> 00:16:50,357
This is it we're done for ever since the
great pirate era started we've been losing

291
00:16:50,440 --> 00:16:53,777
more and more of our people every day the

292
00:16:53,860 --> 00:16:56,297
humans take the mermaids
to sabo odi and sell

293
00:16:56,380 --> 00:16:58,317
them off some of them went missing this

294
00:16:58,400 --> 00:17:01,377
morning i'm telling you
it's just a matter of

295
00:17:01,460 --> 00:17:07,297
time before fishman island falls filthy

296
00:17:07,380 --> 00:17:10,780
humans we gotta kill
them before they kill us

297
00:17:14,640 --> 00:17:17,737
listen up this man
sacrificed his life to blow

298
00:17:17,820 --> 00:17:20,349
up the human shop and
set the Slave's free!

299
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:31,000
Tch, sir's right, stupid humans.

300
00:17:34,120 --> 00:17:36,000
Yeah, that guy's awesome.

301
00:17:36,300 --> 00:17:37,220
Sure is.

302
00:17:37,540 --> 00:17:39,246
Yeah, that's what I wanna be.

303
00:17:39,680 --> 00:17:40,820
Count me in.

304
00:17:45,300 --> 00:17:46,677
Have you heard the news?

305
00:17:46,760 --> 00:17:49,220
Arlong sank another human pirate ship!

306
00:17:50,680 --> 00:17:55,740
Now, I'll tell you about those
wretched worms called humans.

307
00:17:55,940 --> 00:18:00,197
Ages ago, when they realized that we,
the fishmen, were the superior race,

308
00:18:00,280 --> 00:18:02,500
they became jealous and afraid.

309
00:18:03,280 --> 00:18:08,280
And then, they began to
persecute our people.

310
00:18:09,040 --> 00:18:13,100
The human race plagued the entire
world like the vermin they are.

311
00:18:13,320 --> 00:18:16,677
They used their numbers to
gain dominance over our people.

312
00:18:16,760 --> 00:18:20,407
Then all of us fishmen were
driven down here to the sea floor.

313
00:18:20,940 --> 00:18:24,340
Listen to me, and don't forget this.

314
00:18:27,080 --> 00:18:30,917
There's this really nice human name
Rayleigh I made friends with on the surface.

315
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:33,118
And he's not mean like the rest are.

316
00:18:33,220 --> 00:18:36,279
He doesn't even look that
disgusted when he sees me.

317
00:18:36,940 --> 00:18:39,040
Wait, Heart, where are you going?

318
00:18:39,260 --> 00:18:41,613
I don't like your stupid stories, Hachi.

319
00:18:42,360 --> 00:18:43,777
They make me sick.

320
00:18:43,860 --> 00:18:46,820
Humans fear the fishmen.

321
00:18:47,300 --> 00:18:51,060
You must keep the bitterness
of the dead alive, Fruit.

322
00:18:51,780 --> 00:18:53,620
Remember our past.

323
00:18:54,020 --> 00:18:57,300
The very existence of
humanity is pure evil.

324
00:18:59,520 --> 00:19:01,017
You must hate them.

325
00:19:01,100 --> 00:19:02,397
Hate them.

326
00:19:02,480 --> 00:19:03,780
Hate them.

327
00:19:04,200 --> 00:19:05,420
Hate them!

328
00:19:06,800 --> 00:19:08,137
This is terrible!

329
00:19:08,220 --> 00:19:10,380
Tiger's been slain by humans!

330
00:19:10,800 --> 00:19:13,400
The hero of the fishmen is dead! No!

331
00:19:14,240 --> 00:19:16,920
It seems Tiger was not the hero we needed.

332
00:19:25,600 --> 00:19:26,880
Who are you people?

333
00:19:27,120 --> 00:19:28,120
What do you want?

334
00:19:28,280 --> 00:19:30,940
Is it true you gave your blood to humans?

335
00:19:31,680 --> 00:19:32,920
So what if I did?

336
00:19:33,200 --> 00:19:35,040
He was dying, I had to help!

337
00:19:52,920 --> 00:19:56,340
This whole country's mad,
right down to the royal family.

338
00:19:56,800 --> 00:19:59,682
The queen's looking to
make nice with the humans.

339
00:20:00,200 --> 00:20:01,860
How stupid can you be?

340
00:20:05,140 --> 00:20:06,060
Jinbei too.

341
00:20:06,520 --> 00:20:09,108
Heard he joined the
seven warlords recently.

342
00:20:09,240 --> 00:20:13,122
The hour long pirates are the only
ones with any pride these days.

343
00:20:13,240 --> 00:20:14,070
Blatant.

344
00:20:18,460 --> 00:20:20,360
Queen Orohime has been shot!

345
00:20:21,940 --> 00:20:24,340
You see, the humans are evil.

346
00:20:24,840 --> 00:20:27,781
They would even stoop so
low as to kill the queen,

347
00:20:27,920 --> 00:20:30,260
and after she's been so kind to them.

348
00:20:31,140 --> 00:20:34,637
If the royal family is too meek
to hold the humans accountable,

349
00:20:34,720 --> 00:20:37,460
then I can't be loyal
to this kingdom anymore!

350
00:20:37,820 --> 00:20:40,720
I don't want to be ruled
by a bunch of cowards!

351
00:20:41,980 --> 00:20:45,960
The heavens have repaid that
spineless otohime for bowing.

352
00:20:46,180 --> 00:20:50,239
Anyone who wants to forgive humans
deserves a big dose into the head.

353
00:21:11,060 --> 00:21:12,780
I hope you're ready, boys.

354
00:21:12,980 --> 00:21:14,300
It's our time now.

355
00:21:14,720 --> 00:21:18,900
We've been chosen by the heavens,
granted this unstoppable power.

356
00:21:20,460 --> 00:21:22,500
Is that what I think it is?

357
00:21:22,620 --> 00:21:24,091
Those are legendary here.

358
00:21:24,400 --> 00:21:26,520
How did you get your hands on this?

359
00:21:27,020 --> 00:21:29,180
You can duplicate these, can't you?

360
00:21:29,880 --> 00:21:30,710
I'll try.

361
00:21:31,500 --> 00:21:34,676
The people of the Fishman
District must come together.

362
00:21:34,880 --> 00:21:37,020
A proud crusade is about to begin.

363
00:21:37,580 --> 00:21:38,410
No mercy.

364
00:21:38,580 --> 00:21:40,637
We'll kill as many humans as we can.

365
00:21:40,720 --> 00:21:41,955
Until the day we die.

366
00:21:42,600 --> 00:21:44,040
This is our destiny.

367
00:21:44,760 --> 00:21:48,172
We've been chosen by heaven
to bring about the revolution.

368
00:21:48,360 --> 00:21:50,460
The day of reckoning is coming.

369
00:21:55,020 --> 00:21:57,580
This is the end of the
road for all of you.

370
00:21:57,740 --> 00:22:00,077
We've been biding our
time for long enough.

371
00:22:00,160 --> 00:22:02,219
Now we'll take our revenge at last.

372
00:22:17,580 --> 00:22:19,157
We could have stopped all this.

373
00:22:19,240 --> 00:22:24,857
I see now the royal family turned their
eyes away from the fishman district.

374
00:22:24,940 --> 00:22:29,881
In our negligence we allowed it to become
a breeding ground for violence and hatred.

375
00:22:30,940 --> 00:22:35,881
We pretended not to see the resentment that
built up as a result of their isolation.

376
00:22:36,040 --> 00:22:40,099
Even as it descended into lawlessness,
we lived in willful ignorance.

377
00:22:40,540 --> 00:22:41,880
Not so fast.

378
00:22:42,160 --> 00:22:43,117
You going somewhere?

379
00:22:43,200 --> 00:22:44,200
We have to run.

380
00:22:44,740 --> 00:22:46,140
I don't think so.

381
00:22:46,340 --> 00:22:48,897
I thought collecting those
signatures would help,

382
00:22:48,980 --> 00:22:51,274
but I wasn't addressing the true issue.

383
00:22:53,040 --> 00:22:54,557
Please forgive me, Mother.

384
00:22:54,640 --> 00:22:56,000
I'm so sorry.

385
00:22:56,220 --> 00:22:57,257
I know it's difficult,

386
00:22:57,340 --> 00:23:01,800
but you can't pollute the children's
minds with your anger towards humans.

387
00:23:02,220 --> 00:23:03,050
Your resentment.

388
00:23:03,133 --> 00:23:04,394
Do not make it theirs.

389
00:23:05,040 --> 00:23:06,757
But it was too late!

390
00:23:06,840 --> 00:23:11,487
Despite all her pleading, the things she
feared had already been set in motion.

391
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:18,720
The real enemy was the resentment
brewing inside our hearts.

392
00:23:19,180 --> 00:23:21,740
I felt it too, that hatred.

393
00:23:22,040 --> 00:23:26,628
But refusing to admit that, I looked
outward when I should have looked inward.

394
00:23:27,260 --> 00:23:31,257
My mother's true killer was
the grudge that pestered

395
00:23:31,340 --> 00:23:33,987
among our people while
we turned a blind eye!

396
00:23:34,660 --> 00:23:37,440
And I believe she knew
it in that very moment.

397
00:23:38,760 --> 00:23:42,280
My dear children, it
doesn't matter who hurt me.

398
00:23:42,980 --> 00:23:44,360
Don't become angry.

399
00:23:44,780 --> 00:23:46,700
Please, not on my behalf.

400
00:23:47,660 --> 00:23:49,320
Don't submit to resentment.

401
00:23:49,920 --> 00:23:53,744
Don't let hatred get the better
of you, and my name or any other.

402
00:23:54,880 --> 00:24:00,220
I listened to my mother's words, but part
of me wasn't able to let go of my anger.

403
00:24:01,200 --> 00:24:04,240
I couldn't help but hate
humans for killing her.

404
00:24:06,420 --> 00:24:07,460
Me neither.

405
00:24:08,860 --> 00:24:11,000
A person's pain dies with them.

406
00:24:11,600 --> 00:24:16,200
A grudge is created by the living, and
only the living make it grow stronger.

407
00:24:19,180 --> 00:24:23,945
Because of my prejudice, I overlooked what
was happening in the Fishman district.

408
00:24:24,140 --> 00:24:29,060
And by the time I came to my senses, it
was already spiraling out of control.

409
00:24:31,680 --> 00:24:33,560
If we don't do something soon,

410
00:24:33,960 --> 00:24:37,784
the people of Fishman Island will
be done in by their own hatred.

411
00:24:37,900 --> 00:24:40,040
A foe more deadly than any human.

412
00:24:46,980 --> 00:24:48,392
This will be tough, man.

413
00:24:48,480 --> 00:24:50,017
It's not like the island's bubble.

414
00:24:50,100 --> 00:24:52,159
It might shoot right past the Noah.

415
00:24:52,540 --> 00:24:54,577
It needs to get close
enough to surround it.

416
00:24:54,660 --> 00:24:56,120
No more, no less.

417
00:24:57,000 --> 00:24:58,180
Strawhead, please!

418
00:25:04,680 --> 00:25:06,000
Erase our past!

419
00:25:06,460 --> 00:25:08,220
Set us back to zero!

420
00:25:09,220 --> 00:25:13,338
Eradicate the shadows cast by our
grudge so that we may see the light!

421
00:25:17,480 --> 00:25:19,640
Okay, get ready to fire!

422
00:25:20,040 --> 00:25:21,040
I'm on it!

423
00:25:30,220 --> 00:25:31,060
Here we go!

424
00:25:31,760 --> 00:25:34,560
All we can do is start over.

425
00:25:34,880 --> 00:25:36,140
We must!

426
00:25:41,800 --> 00:25:43,920
Would you give it a rest already?

427
00:25:44,200 --> 00:25:46,880
The rage of our people will never die!

428
00:25:51,740 --> 00:25:57,380
Brother Hachi, just let me
do this my way. Trust me.

429
00:25:58,580 --> 00:25:59,800
Hey, wait a second.

430
00:26:00,020 --> 00:26:03,057
Those guys fighting Horty's
crew in the plaza, aren't they?

431
00:26:03,140 --> 00:26:04,360
Yeah, you're right.

432
00:26:04,580 --> 00:26:06,380
They're the Straw Hat Pirates.

433
00:26:06,520 --> 00:26:08,660
And Boss Jinbei too. What?

434
00:26:10,040 --> 00:26:12,360
That's Foofy's place. You're right.

435
00:26:28,320 --> 00:26:29,220
We did it!

436
00:26:29,360 --> 00:26:30,478
It's in the bubble!

437
00:26:33,600 --> 00:26:36,800
Our minds were made up as
soon as we got to the plaza.

438
00:26:37,580 --> 00:26:40,700
With Jinbei's help, we were
gonna save this island.

439
00:26:41,520 --> 00:26:43,108
Leave it to me and my crew.

440
00:26:51,620 --> 00:26:53,679
That's what friends are for, right?

441
00:27:19,360 --> 00:27:23,280
We should never have
suspected him, human or not.

442
00:27:23,700 --> 00:27:24,760
What's the holdup?

443
00:27:25,720 --> 00:27:26,940
We should go!

444
00:27:30,540 --> 00:27:32,257
Hurry up! Run!

445
00:27:32,340 --> 00:27:35,577
I think I'm gonna stay here. What?

446
00:27:35,660 --> 00:27:37,157
Me too!

447
00:27:37,240 --> 00:27:38,217
Yeah!

448
00:27:38,300 --> 00:27:39,397
Same here!

449
00:27:39,480 --> 00:27:41,237
I am not running away!

450
00:27:41,320 --> 00:27:42,280
Me neither!

451
00:27:46,140 --> 00:27:46,970
Luffy!

452
00:27:47,053 --> 00:27:49,060
There's air on the Noah! Yeah!

453
00:27:51,160 --> 00:27:52,317
That may be!

454
00:27:52,400 --> 00:27:55,317
But I'm going to catch you
along before you get there!

455
00:27:55,400 --> 00:27:57,880
What should we do, Luffy? You'll be okay.

456
00:27:58,280 --> 00:28:01,537
Just follow my lead, and I promise
I won't let Heart hurt you.

457
00:28:01,620 --> 00:28:02,580
Yes, right!

458
00:28:13,560 --> 00:28:14,580
Feeling brave?

459
00:28:17,120 --> 00:28:18,200
Careful, Luffy!

460
00:28:20,280 --> 00:28:23,339
That machine's no match for
the spirit of the squid!

461
00:28:25,600 --> 00:28:27,000
It's a spirit!

462
00:28:30,500 --> 00:28:32,240
That's not spirit!

463
00:28:33,500 --> 00:28:35,360
That's just spit!

464
00:28:40,060 --> 00:28:40,940
Ink.

465
00:28:44,680 --> 00:28:48,180
Fortunately, I can copy
myself with squitting.

466
00:28:50,140 --> 00:28:52,640
The spirit of the squid is under...

467
00:28:55,180 --> 00:28:56,010
No!

468
00:28:56,093 --> 00:28:57,404
I don't want to be dried squid!

469
00:28:59,000 --> 00:28:59,830
Wow!

470
00:28:59,913 --> 00:29:01,557
I didn't know your robot
could shoot fireballs!

471
00:29:01,640 --> 00:29:03,934
How many cool attacks can this baby do?

472
00:29:07,280 --> 00:29:08,110
Wait!

473
00:29:08,193 --> 00:29:09,023
That came out of you?

474
00:29:09,106 --> 00:29:11,757
You really shouldn't have let
your guard down, little guy!

475
00:29:11,840 --> 00:29:12,897
Yeah, like I would.

476
00:29:12,980 --> 00:29:13,810
Wait, Paul!

477
00:29:13,893 --> 00:29:14,723
Be shot!

478
00:29:16,100 --> 00:29:16,930
Be gone!

479
00:29:19,760 --> 00:29:22,540
Who uses their bare hand to stop a hammer?

480
00:29:26,900 --> 00:29:31,640
On second thought, I probably could have
found a less painful way to do that.

481
00:29:31,800 --> 00:29:35,797
Hey, Chopper, I thought that one was
supposed to be your normal-looking form.

482
00:29:35,880 --> 00:29:37,939
Sure you're okay looking so freaky?

483
00:29:38,420 --> 00:29:39,657
I don't care anymore.

484
00:29:39,740 --> 00:29:43,797
I wanted to look human before,
because I didn't have any friends.

485
00:29:43,880 --> 00:29:48,580
But now, I want to be a monster
so I can help Luffy. Gotcha.

486
00:29:49,180 --> 00:29:52,080
I'll slice that smile right off your face!

487
00:29:59,500 --> 00:30:03,160
Bring me the real strongest
swordsman on Fishman Island.

488
00:30:06,160 --> 00:30:07,700
There's no way it's you.

489
00:30:07,880 --> 00:30:09,527
I didn't even break a sweat.

490
00:30:09,700 --> 00:30:11,000
Got you now!

491
00:30:13,880 --> 00:30:16,060
I'm sorry, but your time is over.

492
00:30:18,860 --> 00:30:21,020
Did you hear a word that I said?

493
00:30:21,440 --> 00:30:22,960
I'm gonna save them all!

494
00:30:23,120 --> 00:30:25,700
From you and anything you've got!
